      </sec>
      <sec id="article-23704.s10" sec-type="Differential Diagnosis">
        <title>Differential Diagnosis</title>
        <p>Other conditions that present with pruritus without a rash and elevated bile acids should be considered in the differential diagnosis (see <bold>Table 2</bold>). Appropriate clinical evaluation, laboratory testing, and history are essential to distinguish these conditions from intrahepatic cholestasis of pregnancy and guide management.<xref ref-type="bibr" rid="article-23704.r4">[4]</xref></p>
        <table-wrap id="article-23704.table1" position="float" orientation="portrait">
